course: dictionary
lesson: 10378
title: A treaty is a written promise between nations
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A treaty is a written agreement between countries or nations. You can find its meaning from the words around it: «After the Battle of Kadesh, Egypt and the Hittites signed one of the oldest known peace treaties.» Signed and peace tell you the two sides agreed to stop fighting, so a peace treaty is a written agreement to end a war.
explain: Look for promises as clues: «New Zealand still works to keep the treaty's promises.» A treaty has promises in it, and the countries that sign it must keep them. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Egypt and the Hittites signed a written agreement to stop fighting" still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Treaties can be broken, and two versions can say different things. «In 1840 many Māori chiefs and the British Crown signed the Treaty of Waitangi, but the English and Māori texts said different things about who held power.» When you read a treaty, ask who wrote it and who it was for.
fact: A treaty is a written agreement between countries or nations.
fact: A peace treaty is a treaty that agrees to end a war.
fact: To sign a treaty means to write your name on it to show you agree. To break a treaty means not to keep its promises.
fact: The Treaty of Waitangi was signed in 1840 by many Māori chiefs and the British Crown. Waitangi Day, 6 February, is New Zealand's national day.
fact: Treaties is the plural of treaty.
exercise: «After the Battle of Kadesh, Egypt and the Hittites signed one of the oldest known peace treaties.» What is a peace treaty? | *A written agreement to end a war | A kind of food | A long walk to the palace | A battle with swords and shields
exercise: Which word is the plural of treaty? | treatys | treats | *treaties | treatyes
exercise: What does it mean to sign a treaty? | To tear it up and throw it away | *To agree to it by writing your name on it | To paint a picture of it | To read it aloud in a loud voice
test: What did the students in Beijing feel about the treaty? | They were happy, so they held a party | They wanted to sign the treaty themselves | *They were angry that China did not get its old rights back | They had never heard of China
test: A treaty is a ____ between countries. | *written agreement | race | football match | shopping list
exam: What does a treaty between two nations usually do? | *Sets out agreed promises that both nations keep | Changes the weather | Joins a boat race | Lets children skip school
